-- title:
--   Velocity fields generated by box motions
-- statement:
--   This is part of the construction of smooth forced incompressible Navier–Stokes flows on $\mathbb R^3$ whose fluid particles simulate a Turing machine: a fixed particle enters a fixed box exactly when the machine halts. A field is a function $v(t,x)$ of time $t\in\mathbb R$ and position $x\in\mathbb R^3$, and a velocity is a field with values in $\mathbb R^3$.
--
--   A box layout assigns to each index $i$ of a finite set a centre $c_i\in\mathbb R^3$ and half-widths $w_i\in\mathbb R^3$, describing the box $\prod_k[c_{ik}-w_{ik},c_{ik}+w_{ik}]$.
--
--   1. **Solid boxes.** The closed box $[c_i-w_i,c_i+w_i]$ of layout $A$.
--   2. **Affine maps.** The map sending box $i$ of $A$ to box $i$ of $B$, given by $x\mapsto c^B_i+\frac{w^B_i}{w^A_i}(x-c^A_i)$ coordinatewise.
--   3. **Time rescaling.** For a box motion from $A$ to $B$, the field centre and field scale of box $i$ at time $t$ are $c_i(2t-\frac12)$ and $w_i(2t-\frac12)/w^A_i$. So the motion takes place during $\frac14\le t\le\frac34$.
--   4. **Velocity.** The sum over $i$ of the moving-box velocities of the reference boxes $[-w^A_i,w^A_i]$, moved by these centres and scales, with margin $\eta$.
--   5. **Paths.** The affine path of the label $x-c^A_i$ under the centre and scale of box $i$. It describes how a point of box $i$ moves.
